    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>People</h2>
      <p class="lede">Ask me what I’m most proud of and I’ll point you here every time.</p>
      <p class="intro">People work is the hardest kind to document because the evidence lives in people, not pages. It shows up in relationships that have lasted years past any job title, in team members who still reach out long after the role ended, and in the quiet moments when someone tells you a conversation changed something for them.</p>
      <p class="intro" style="margin-bottom:2.5rem">I listen. I ask questions that get to the underside of things. I’ve coached direct reports through finding their voice, and I’ve been the person in the room asserting the needs of the business to shareholders and vendors, with clarity and care when the stakes were high. I approach every working relationship with empathy, curiosity, and genuine respect for the individual.</p>
      <div class="quotes">
        <blockquote>“The relationships we nurture are really what matters in life, and you’ve left a trail of so much kindness and uplifting support behind you through Dreamers & Doers.”</blockquote>
        <blockquote>“Empathy IS YOUR SUPERPOWER! And I’m so lucky to have witnessed it and felt it. So much of the art of how you do this is by leading by example.”</blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="content">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Content</h2>
      <p class="lede">Published work has a different kind of energy.</p>
      <p class="intro">It went through hands other than mine, an editor, a brand, an audience, and came out the other side still feeling like something worth reading.</p>
      <div class="formats">
        <div><h3>White papers</h3><em>The best white papers don’t feel like homework.</em><p>I shape the research, find the narrative thread, and write content that earns its read instead of sitting in a downloads folder.</p></div>
        <div><h3>One pagers</h3><em>The smallest format does the heaviest lifting.</em><p>I find the sharpest version of the story and make sure it lands before the page runs out.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Articles</h3><em>The goal isn’t to add more meaning, it’s to reveal what’s already there.</em><p>Interviews, features, and ongoing content ecosystems, built by turning conversations and raw input into structured storytelling.</p></div>
        <div><h3>Campaigns</h3><em>Strong marketing doesn’t feel louder. It feels aligned.</em><p>Marketing and campaign materials that preserve meaning while making ideas easier to understand and act on.</p></div>
